        "original_id": "7056577d-348a-593a-884e-bc6c07db029d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mario Lemieux\n- Teams: Pittsburgh Penguins, Chicago Blackhawks\n- Events: 1992 Stanley Cup Finals\n- Organizations: NHL\n- Music groups: Comeback Kid\n\nFacts:\n- Mario Lemieux was born on October 5, 1965, and he is a Canadian former professional ice hockey player.\n- Mario Lemieux is the current owner of the Pittsburgh Penguins team.\n- In the 1992 Stanley Cup Finals, the Chicago Blackhawks took an early 4–1 lead in Game 1 before Mario Lemieux and the Pittsburgh Penguins came back to win the game.\n- In the 1992 Stanley Cup Finals, the Pittsburgh Penguins swept the Chicago Blackhawks in four games and won their second consecutive and second overall Stanley Cup.\n- The band Comeback Kid took its name from a newspaper headline about Mario Lemieux returning to the NHL.",
